### Bad Code Snippet (Vulnerable)

```java
import java.sql.Connection;
import java.sql.DriverManager;

public class VulnerableExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        // Connect to the database using DriverManager.getConnection()
        String url = "jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/mydatabase";
        String user = "username";
        String password = "password";

        Connection conn = DriverManager.getConnection(url, user, password);

        // Execute a query without parameterization
        String sql = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = 'admin'";
        Statement stmt = conn.createStatement();
        ResultSet rs = stmt.executeQuery(sql);

        while(rs.next()) {
            System.out.println("User found!");
        }

        // Close resources
        rs.close();
        stmt.close();
        conn.close();
    }
}
```

### Good Code Snippet

```java
import java.sql.Connection;
import java.sql.DriverManager;
import java.sql.PreparedStatement;

public class SecureExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        // Connect to the database using DriverManager.getConnection()
        String url = "jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/mydatabase";
        String user = "username";
        String password = "password";

        Connection conn = DriverManager.getConnection(url, user, password);

        // Use PreparedStatement for prepared statements to prevent SQL injection
        String sql = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = ?";
        PreparedStatement pstmt = conn.prepareStatement(sql);

        // Set parameters before executing the statement
        pstmt.setString(1, "admin");

        // Execute the statement
        ResultSet rs = pstmt.executeQuery();

        while(rs.next()) {
            System.out.println("User found!");
        }

        // Close resources
        rs.close();
        pstmt.close();
        conn.close();
    }
}
```

In the bad code snippet, we directly execute a SQL query without any parameterization, which makes it vulnerable to SQL injection attacks if the input from the user is not properly sanitized or validated. The good code snippet uses `PreparedStatement`, which allows us to safely pass values into the query string, preventing SQL injection attacks.

